# Line endings
#
# Text is stored LF in the repository and checked out CRLF, which is what
# this project already does by way of core.autocrlf. Stating it here makes
# it a property of the repository rather than of each contributor's Git
# config, so a checkout is consistent either way -- and an editor or script
# that writes the "wrong" endings can no longer turn a one-line change into
# a whole-file diff.
#
# text=auto lets Git decide what is text; anything it detects as binary is
# left alone. Do not add an `eol` override for a path you want left as-is:
# `eol` implies textness, so it wins over `-text` and forces conversion.
*   text=auto eol=crlf
